  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Uganda - Larvae production facility</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With a DGGF Start-up Loan Marula Agribusiness B.V. (Marula) will be able to further develop the existing larvae production facility together with the local subsidiary Marula ProTeen: a nursery and processing facility (based on circular waste) for Black Soldier larvae (maggots), which will be used as protein and fat component in animal feed . The residual waste will be used as fertilizer for agriculture in Uganda.The pilot of the local company started at the beginning of 2018 with the help of a DGGF Technical Assistance subsidy and has been successfully concluded. Marula therefore wants to expand the current production capacity. The impact of this project is multiple, it offers a solution to the major waste problem in the country and also ensures a reliable and affordable component for animal feed  and thereby contributes to reliable food consumption. The production and processing facility also provides additional employment (growth of 50 people).</narrative>
  </description>
